  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool (config_005) is the current best at 0.650 acc, and image-only with resnet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208 acc. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the image modality contributes complementary information when fused with the strong RNA signal, or whether it will dilute performance. This experiment (config_030) tests multimodal fusion by adding resnet50 image features via concat to the best-validated RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), changing only the modality and fusion while holding all RNA-side settings at their proven optimum. It is the best use of the next experiment because it answers the single most consequential design question—whether a multimodal strategy is worth pursuing at all—before committing budget to more complex fusion variants or alternative image encoders. If it beats 0.650, we justify exploring ViT-L and weighted fusion; if it underperforms, we can redirect budget to RNA-only refinements or a stronger image encoder."
}

